WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
[music playing]

00:00:03.033 --> 00:00:07.870
So this robot learns in simulation to execute a&nbsp;
lot of different, diverse walking styles and then&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.870 --> 00:00:13.390
we take it out into the real world and it can walk,&nbsp;
it can hop, it can duck underneath obstacles, it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.390 --> 00:00:18.250
can climb over obstacles. Really the concept is&nbsp;
that locomotion is sort of under-specified so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.250 --> 00:00:22.570
if I told you to just walk forward you could&nbsp;
do it in a lot of different ways and it's the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.570 --> 00:00:26.650
same thing for these sort of learning agents. If&nbsp;
we give them a set of instructions but we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.650 --> 00:00:30.190
don't tell them exactly how to solve the problem,&nbsp;
they could solve it in a lot of different ways

